| NiGHT-SCANNER V1.O / Complete User Documentation / by nocTurne deSign/OGN |
`-------------------/-----------------------------/-------------------------'

.---------.
| SUMMARY |
`---------'
 NiGHT-SCANNER  is  a fast and easy to use new-files/files-reverse door for
 AmiExpress.    Seeing  that  everyone  and their mothers have coded such a
 program,  I  decided  to  join  this growing trend.  However NiGHT-SCANNER
 offers  time-saving  features  and  configurability missing in most of the
 others.    Continue  reading to learn of these many features and become an
 elite  pro  at  using  NiGHT-SCANNER.   Amaze your comrades!  Impress your
 girlfriend(s)!

.-----------.
| ARGUMENTS |
`-----------'
 NiGHT-SCANNER  may  be  initiated  from  the command  line with arguments.  
 Following  are  the templates and complete explanation of these arguments,
 as well as some examples:

 Command templates:  "N <date> <directory>"  - show files of <date>
                     "N <special>"           - do something special
                     "F <directory>"         - show all files               
                     "FR <directory"         - show files in reverse                 
 
  The <date> argument may be one of the following:

    `XX-XX(-XX)' - Since a specific MONTH-DATE(-YEAR)
            `-x' - Since x days ago (x may be multiple digits)
             `S' - Since the date of your last logon
             `T' - Since midnite today
             `Y' - Since midnite yesterday

  The <directory> argument may be:

             `x' - Directory number x (may be multi-digit)
             `U' - Upload directory (default if not specified)
             `A' - All directories
             `H' - Hold directory (with proper access)

  <special> may be:

             `E' - Open the configuration menu
             `?' - Get online quick help
             `Z' - Download this file

  Usage examples:

          "N S" - List files in the upload dir since your last call.
        "N S U" - Identical to the above
          "N Y" - List files since yesterday
      "N -97 2" - List files since 97 days ago in directory 2
      "N 11-10" - List files in the upload dir since November 10th
                  of THIS year
   "N 11-10-93" - List files in the upload dir since November 10th
                  of 1993
           "FR" - Show files in the upload directory backwards
        "FR 12" - List directory twelve in reverse
        "N T H" - List today's files in the upload directory
          "N E" - Edit your personal configuration


.---------------------------------.
| Date/Dir Prompts for `N' search |
`---------------------------------'
 If  you  do not specify the <date> argument you will be greeted with a date
 prompt.  By default the date string is the current date.  Using the '<' and
 '>'  keys you can decrease/increase this date by increments of one day.  If
 you  wish to enter a completely new string, simply start typing.  The entry
 field  is somewhat intelligent.  If you enter '6' as the first character in
 the  month,  it will be mapped to '06'.  There is no need for hyphens to be
 typed.  'Q' may be entered at any time to immediately exit the door.

 After  a  valid  date  has  been  entered,  you  will be asked to enter the
 directory  to  scan.    You may choose to search a specific dir number, the
 'U'pload dir, the 'H'old dir, or 'A'LL directories.


.---------------------.
| Pause Mode Features |
`---------------------'
 At  this  point  the directory will be loaded and searched.  If files since
 the  given date are found they will be displayed.  When a screenful of text
 has appeared, NiGHT-SCANNER will go into pause mode at which point you have
 a variety of options:

 `Y' - Continue listing files.
 `N' - Stop listing files.
 `Q' - Same as above.
 `NS' - Show files non-stop (abort with CTRL-C)
 
 `F' - Flag Files:
 A  large  text field will be opened so that you may flag multiple filenames
 (or  filenumbers if you have that config option turned on) for downloading.
 CTRL-X  will  clear  the field.  Filenames/numbers must be separated by a a
 space.

 `?' - Key command list:
 This  will  list  the sysop-configured key commands available to you if you
 have  the  appropriate  access   level.      You   may   run doors (nukers,
 file-viewers,  or whatever the sysop has chosen) from within NiGHT-SCANNER.
 If,  for instance, 'X' has been assigned to a nuke program, pressing 'X' at
 the  pause  prompt  will  spawn  the  nuker  so that you may dispose of any
 unwanted files you may have seen.  If the sysop has set, an argument prompt
 will  first  appear  so  that you may enter  the names or numbers of files, 
 separated by spaces,  if the spawned  door supports them.   When the  child 
 door exits you will be returned to the pause prompt.
 
 When  you  exit NiGHT-SCANNER, the number of files and bytes listed will be
 shown, as well the number of files flagged.

 
.---------------------------.
| Configuring NiGHT-SCANNER | 
`---------------------------'
 NiGHT-SCANNER  allows you to define your own personal configuration.  Each
 config  option  may  be  toggled by typing its respective number.  To save
 your configuration simply type 'S'.  To quit type 'Q'.   The following are
 the options you may set:
 
 1) Pause between entries

 If  this is set, after every file entry shown NiGHT-SCANNER will pause.  At
 that  point  you may type 'F' to immediately flag the file shown, or Return
 to continue.
 ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 2) `N' equals `N S U'
 
 If this option is set, you will need only to type 'N' to see the new files
 since your last login.
 ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 3) Use color in the listing

 This will simply add a bit of color to the sizes, dates, etc.. of files
 Nuked file descriptions will appear in blue.
 ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 4) Use dividers between entries

 A  sysop-defined  divider  will  be used between each file-entry if this is
 selected, making for easier reading.
 ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 5) Use date dividers

 If  selected,  sysop-defined  divider  texts  will separate files each time
 there is a date change.
 ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 6) Clear screen after pause
 
 This will simply wipe the screen after every pause prompt.
 ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 7) Use file-numbering system
 
 If  this  is  set,  NiGHT-SCANNER will assign a number to each of the files
 listed  so  that they may be flagged easier.  The listing will be truncated
 however,  so  the  years of the files and the file-test results will not be
 shown.
 ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 8) Show only whole descriptions
 
 If, while showing files, the next description would not be shown completely
 (as  it  would exceed your lines/screen setting), the listing will pause if
 this option is set.  Try it to understand its usefulness.
 ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 9) Omit sent-by lines
 
 This will simply omit the last line of each description.


